    "question": "Can connected workspaces (Slack, Teams, Jira) reveal where hidden adopters work, without false positives?",
    "finding": "Naive matching attributes 632 hidden users at 67% precision and creates 3 phantom sales-ready accounts. The worst naive error: 'Arworth Hiking Club' put 18 unrelated users into Arworth Retail. Guarded matching attributes 329 at 100% precision, recovers 34% of hidden employees, and adds 19 genuinely sales-ready accounts with 0 phantoms. Trust a workspace's verified domain; treat names as clues that need a colleague to corroborate them; drop guests and any workspace whose members already resolve to several companies. Synthetic data makes the guards look perfect; in production, audit a sample of attributions by hand each quarter.",
    "caveat": "Workspace metadata is personal context: use it only in aggregate at the account level, within the permissions users granted, and never to contact an individual about a side project."
  },
